# Strumming: Down-Up Eighths (repertoire plan: st-strum-eighths). Your part: Em (022000) for
# 2 bars, D (xx0232; strum strings 4 to 1 only) for 2, four times: 16 bars of eighth notes, down
# on 1 2 3 4 and up on every "and". The hand never stops: it moves down and up all the time,
# and only the direction tells you where the beat is. Bars 9-16: accent beats 2 and 4 (a little
# harder down-strum on "two" and "four"). The last bar ends on a held D on beat 3.
# The teacher plays an original tune over the chords (E minor, without C or C#). Its notes on
# beats 1 and 3 are always notes of the chord in force. It ends on D over the D chord, an open
# ending that leads straight back to bar 1 when you loop the study.
title: Strumming: Down-Up Eighths
